  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-MYS102</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting decent work fairer, more resilient and sustainable supply chains going forward</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Based on DWCP 2019-2025, under DWCP Priority 1, Outcome 1, Output 1.1.4, the ILO has been supporting constituents in Malaysia towards improved harmonious industrial relations and social dialogue institutions and processes, including through reviews and strengthening of the Industrial Court, National Labour Advisory Council and National Wages Consultative Council as well as with respect to specific sectors and supply chains.

For instance, under the current Development Cooperation project titled &quot;Building Responsible Value Chains in Asia through the Promotion of Decent Work in Business Operations (Phase II), the ILO focus is provision of technical support on the promotion of Responsible Business Conduct (RBC) and the labour dimension of Human Rights (HRDD) to achieve decent work in supply chains. The ultimate goal is to promote inclusive, responsible and sustainable enterprises and decent work in supply chains in the specific sectors in Malaysia.

Partners include the tripartite constituents in Malaysia, Japan External Trade Organization (JETRO) and Japan Federation of Labour and Social Security Attorney&apos;s Associations (for Japan component) - for activities in Japan. 

The target beneficiaries are: Government ministries, Employers organization, Workers organization, Multinational Enterprises and SMEs, Academic institutions, Attorney&apos;s associations, other local institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
